M6 PR 8b before/after check (docs/plans/m6-pr8b-envelope.md, D5) and size re-measurement (D4, D3)
Question: does the band reduction change anything but the two fill collections of an envelope over
more than ENVELOPE_COLUMNS + 1 = 901 frames?
date: 2026-10-03
Both halves use the worktree's own .venv (Python-only change: _core and plugins are the same build,
build/python, from `just python` at d436627). No main-checkout state is involved.
before half: run at d436627 (the plan commit; python/ and tests/ equal to 8055ce7), before any product edit.
after half:  run at 4e9730a (the reduction and its tests).
script: scratchpad before_after.py (prepare / run HALF / compare). After the after half first ran, only its
compare step changed: the fill-group span is matched by <g> depth (matplotlib 3.11 nests a clip-path <g>
inside each group), and stdout paths are normalized (each half prints its own output directory).

== inputs (produced once, by `before_after.py prepare`, read by both halves)
scenario logs (astra.scenario.run): elevator_step, atmosphere_ceiling_halt;
the descent batch (tests/python/mc_analysis_fixtures/descent_batch.yaml, 24 runs; 500 and 50 frames);
R9's batch (tests/python/mc_planted_fixtures/planted.yaml, 130 runs of 10 s; 10,000 frames).

== outputs, per half (cwd = the worktree, the installed .venv/bin/astra), 19 commands
astra plot LOG PACKAGE --out DIR, for LOG in {elevator_step, atmosphere_ceiling_halt} and PACKAGE in
  {flight, attitude, health, aircraft/_template/plots/{controls,ground_track,wrench}.yaml,
  aircraft/notional_transport/plots/cruise.yaml}                                       (14)
astra mc analyze descent --signal v0.derived.altitude --signal v0.slow_rate.value       (1)
astra mc analyze r9 --criterion 'max.v0.derived.alpha > 0.23'
  --signal v0.derived.alpha --signal v0.derived.altitude                                (1)
astra report elevator_step.h5; astra report descent (both signals); astra report r9 (criterion,
  both signals)                                                                         (3)
Each command's stdout is kept and compared.

== rules
- every exit code equal;
- a file with no fill group: byte-identical (cmp);
- a file with fill groups (<g id="[fig<k>-]FillBetweenPolyCollection_<n>">, each holding exactly one
  <path>, one <use> and one nested <g>): the same group ids in both halves, 2 per envelope; either
  byte-identical, or identical once each group's byte span (start tag through its depth-matched </g>)
  is replaced by a fixed placeholder, with every group smaller after;
- containment on R9's batch (after half): test_mc_analysis._band_at reads each drawn band's path, and
  every frame's min..max and 5..95 % values lie inside it.

